# G9 (graphics): Save As in the file dialog. It starts with the document's name selected and the folder it is in; changing the type
# swaps the extension; New folder opens its box and Esc closes it; a read-only file is refused; a name that is there asks before it is
# replaced (No is the default); a new name saves, and the scenario ends there, because DOS dates what a run writes with the real clock.
# Every frame's CRC-32 must equal the host's in both graphics modes.
@dialog
@dir QUILL
@place Quill C:\QUILL
@cwd C:\DOCS
@dir DOCS\LETTERS
@copy letter.qld DOCS\
@copy letter.rtf DOCS\
@copy plain.qld DOCS\
@stamp DOCS\LETTER.QLD 2026-11-24 18:45
@stamp DOCS\LETTER.RTF 2026-11-02 09:05
@stamp DOCS\PLAIN.QLD 2026-03-14 12:00
@readonly DOCS\PLAIN.QLD
@open C:\DOCS\LETTER.QLD
f10 down down down enter      # File > Save As...: LETTER.QLD, selected
altf                          # New folder: its box
esc                           # closed
altn p l a i n period q l d enter   # PLAIN.QLD is read-only
enter                         # OK
altn end bspace bspace bspace bspace bspace bspace bspace bspace bspace   # the name emptied
l e t t e r period r t f enter   # LETTER.RTF is there: Do you want to replace it?
tab                           # the other button
tab                           # and back
enter                         # No is the default: back to the dialog
altt down                     # Save as type: Rich Text Format
altn end bspace bspace bspace bspace bspace bspace bspace bspace bspace bspace   # the name emptied
n e w enter                   # NEW.RTF: saved
